  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] (f : E → ℝ),\n  Differentiable ℝ f →\n    ∀ (eta beta B ell : ℝ),\n      0 < eta →\n        ∀ (hbeta : 0 < beta),\n          0 < B →\n            2 ≤ ell →\n              0 < ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) →\n                LipschitzWith ⟨beta, LT.lt.le hbeta⟩ (gradient f) →\n                  ∀ (x0 xp : E),\n                    ‖x0 - eta • gradient f xp - xp‖ ≤ √(↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta) →\n                      64 * beta ^ 2 * (ell * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) / B + ell ^ 2) ≤ 1 / eta ^ 2 →\n                        have h := x0 - eta • gradient f xp;\n                        have q := MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => h + √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n                        have P := MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n                        have nu := (MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Ioc 0 1)).prod P;\n                        have m := fun x =>\n                          ∫ (a : ℝ × E),\n                            Inner.inner ℝ\n                              ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                                (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • ((x, a).1 - h) -\n                                  Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • (x, a).2.2))\n                              (gradient f xp -\n                                gradient f\n                                  (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • ((x, a).1 - h) +\n                                    Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • (x, a).2.2)) ∂nu;\n                        have mB := fun x =>\n                          ∫ (a : ℝ × E),\n                            Min.min B\n                              (Max.max (-B)\n                                (Inner.inner ℝ\n                                  ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                                    (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • ((x, a).1 - h) -\n                                      Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • (x, a).2.2))\n                                  (gradient f xp -\n                                    gradient f\n                                      (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • ((x, a).1 - h) +\n                                        Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • (x, a).2.2)))) ∂nu;\n                        have V := fun x =>\n                          ∫ (a : ℝ × E),\n                            Max.max\n                              (|Inner.inner ℝ\n                                    ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                                      (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • ((x, a).1 - h) -\n                                        Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • (x, a).2.2))\n                                    (gradient f xp -\n                                      gradient f\n                                        (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • ((x, a).1 - h) +\n                                          Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * (x, a).2.1) • (x, a).2.2))| -\n                                B)\n                              0 ∂nu;\n                        have qhat := q.tilted mB;\n                        have K :=\n                          Min.min (B ^ 2 / (40 * beta ^ 2 * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta ^ 2)) (B / (8 * beta * eta));\n                        Measurable m ∧\n                          Measurable mB ∧\n                            Measurable V ∧\n                              (∀ (x : E), 0 ≤ V x ∧ |m x - mB x| ≤ V x) ∧\n                                MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (2 * ell * V x) - 1) q ∧\n                                  ∫ (x : E), Real.exp (2 * ell * V x) - 1 ∂q ≤ 2 * Real.exp (-K) ∧\n                                    MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (2 * ell * V x) - 1) qhat ∧\n                                      ∫ (x : E), Real.exp (2 * ell * V x) - 1 ∂qhat ≤ 2 * Real.exp (2 * B - K) ∧\n                                        MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (2 * ell * |m x - mB x|) - 1) qhat ∧\n                                          ∫ (x : E), Real.exp (2 * ell * |m x - mB x|) - 1 ∂qhat ≤\n                                            2 * Real.exp (2 * B - K)",
    "statement_sha256": "843d4191286cdbfcfe2db87cd1c1c356f19331776f2757fa3cd9e1a660fe413c",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability measure. Measure.map denotes pushforward and Measure.prod independent product.",
      "volume is canonical Lebesgue measure on the finite-dimensional real inner-product space; restricted real volume on Ioc(0,1) is the uniform probability law. Endpoints have zero mass.",
      "gradient f is the actual real inner-product gradient. Differentiable means differentiability everywhere. LipschitzWith beta is the global distance bound, and NNReal denotes nonnegative real numbers.",
      "Integrable asserts Bochner integrability. The displayed real integrals are the typed signed Bochner integrals. ENNReal.ofReal maps a real number to its nonnegative part in the extended nonnegative reals.",
      "Measure.withDensity mu d multiplies mu by the extended-nonnegative density d. Measure.tilted mu m is the exponential tilt with density ofReal(exp(m)/integral exp(m) dmu).",
      "The local scalar estimator definition has been expanded from the compiled theorem type and checked with Lean Meta.isDefEq. All let-bound quantities retain their displayed scopes."
